<h1>Project Architecture & System Evolution</h1>
<div class="subtitle"><strong>Project:</strong> Code Summarization Using AST, PDG, NLP & Green Computing<br><strong>Author / Student:</strong> K. Leela Krishna (24CSB0A30)</div>

<div class="callout">
    <strong>Document Objective:</strong> This document presents two distinct architectural blueprints for this project in clear, humanized terms:
    <ol style="margin-top: 6px; margin-bottom: 0;">
        <li><strong>Architecture 1: Existing System (Current Baseline)</strong> &mdash; How the current code works, step-by-step, and its technical limitations.</li>
        <li><strong>Architecture 2: Proposed Agentic System (Target State)</strong> &mdash; The enhanced design featuring 4 Autonomous AI Agents, Self-Healing error recovery, Green Code Refactoring (Before vs. After), Multi-Level Summaries, and an Interactive Moving PDG Graph.</li>
    </ol>
</div>

<hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; margin: 30px 0;">

<h2>PART 1: The Existing System Architecture</h2>

<p>In simple terms, the existing system is like a <strong>one-way conveyor belt</strong>. You place a piece of Python code at the start, it runs through three fixed tools one by one, and it outputs a short explanation along with a static energy estimate.</p>

<div class="diagram-box">
========================================================================================
                          EXISTING SYSTEM: 4-STAGE LINEAR PIPELINE
========================================================================================

 [ User Python Code ] 
          │
          ▼
 [ 1. Standard Python Parser (ast.parse) ]
          │ 
          ├───► If Syntax / Indentation Error ──► [ ❌ PIPELINE CRASHES WITH RED ERROR ]
          │
          ▼ (If code is syntactically valid)
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │ 2. STATIC FEATURE EXTRACTION                                                       │
 │    • AST Extractor  (ast_extractor.py)  ──► Extracts function names, args, loops   │
 │    • PDG Extractor  (pdg_extractor.py)  ──► Captures Control & Data text edges     │
 │    • Green Profiler (green_computing.py)──► Counts loops & estimates kWh / CO2     │
 └────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                  │
                                  ▼
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │ 3. SINGLE-SHOT AI PROMPT (model_pipeline.py)                                       │
 │    Prompt = Code + Extracted PDG text                                              │
 │    • Calls Groq / HuggingFace API (or AST rule fallback)                           │
 │    • Produces: 1 generic summary sentence                                         │
 └────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                  │
                                  ▼
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │ 4. PRESENTATION SCREEN (gui_app.py)                                                │
 │    • Displays the single summary sentence                                          │
 │    • Static Eco-score number & basic Streamlit bar charts                          │
 │    • Fixed, non-interactive Graphviz dependency circle diagram                     │
 └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
========================================================================================
</div>

<h3>How the Existing Components Work (In Plain English):</h3>

<ol>
    <li><strong>Input & AST Parsing:</strong> When you provide code, Python's built-in parser reads the grammatical structure. It produces an <em>Abstract Syntax Tree</em> (the code's skeleton). 
    <br><em>Problem:</em> If the user misses a single colon or quotation mark, the program crashes instantly without trying to understand what the user meant.</li>
    
    <li><strong>PDG Dependency Extraction:</strong> It scans the code to see which lines depend on other lines (e.g., Line 5 needs the variable calculated at Line 2). It writes these dependencies out as plain text sentences.</li>
    
    <li><strong>Single-Shot LLM Call:</strong> It packs the code and dependencies into one big prompt and sends it to an open-source model (like Llama 3.1 or Qwen 2.5). The model responds once with a 1-to-2 sentence summary.
    <br><em>Problem:</em> The model doesn't check if its answer was accurate, and it only produces one fixed type of summary.</li>
    
    <li><strong>Green Computing Profiler:</strong> It counts loops, nested levels, and file reads. It uses a mathematical formula to assign an Eco Score out of 100.
    <br><em>Problem:</em> It tells you your code is slow or power-wasting, but it cannot fix the code for you.</li>
</ol>

<div class="callout-amber">
    <strong>Summary of Existing Bottlenecks:</strong>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Fragile:</strong> Unhandled syntax typos cause hard crashes.</li>
        <li><strong>Passive:</strong> The AI only speaks when spoken to; it does not verify or self-correct.</li>
        <li><strong>Diagnostic only:</strong> Flags inefficient code, but cannot rewrite it into an efficient version.</li>
        <li><strong>Static UI:</strong> The dependency graph is a flat image that users cannot drag, zoom, or interact with.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; margin: 40px 0;">

<h2>PART 2: The Proposed Agentic System Architecture</h2>

<p>Instead of a rigid one-way script, the proposed architecture introduces an <strong>Autonomous Multi-Agent Team</strong>. Think of it as a team of 5 specialized digital engineers sitting in a room together, collaborating, testing, and improving your code.</p>

<div class="diagram-box">
========================================================================================
                  PROPOSED SYSTEM: AUTONOMOUS MULTI-AGENT ARCHITECTURE
========================================================================================

                       [ User Enters Code (May have errors) ]
                                         │
                                         ▼
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │ STAGE 1: INGESTION & SELF-HEALING GUARD                                            │
 │                                                                                    │
 │   Does the code have a syntax / indentation error?                                 │
 │        ├──► YES: 🩹 AGENT 0 (Self-Healing Agent)                                   │
 │        │         • Reads traceback & line error                                    │
 │        │         • Autonomously fixes missing colon, quote, or indent              │
 │        │         • Sends alert: "Self-healed 1 syntax typo at line 4"              │
 │        │                                                                           │
 │        └──► NO:  Proceeds directly                                                 │
 └───────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                         │ Clean, Validated Code
                                         ▼
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │ STAGE 2: MULTI-AGENT COLLABORATION ENGINE                                          │
 │                                                                                    │
 │  ┌─────────────────────────────────┐       ┌────────────────────────────────────┐  │
 │  │ 🕵️ AGENT 1: Structural Inspector │       │ 🌿 AGENT 2: Green Computing Auditor│  │
 │  │ • Extracts AST tree & functions │       │ • Analyzes loop depths & recursion │  │
 │  │ • Maps Control & Data flow edges│──────►│ • Calculates baseline Eco Score    │  │
 │  │ • Produces: Structural Dossier  │       │ • Produces: Carbon & Energy Audit  │  │
 │  └────────────────┬────────────────┘       └─────────────────┬──────────────────┘  │
 │                   │                                          │                     │
 │                   ├──────────────────┬───────────────────────┤                     │
 │                   ▼                  │                       ▼                     │
 │  ┌─────────────────────────────────┐ │     ┌────────────────────────────────────┐  │
 │  │ ✍️ AGENT 3: Multi-Level         │ │     │ ⚡ AGENT 4: Green Optimizer        │  │
 │  │    Summarizer                   │ │     │    & Verifier                      │  │
 │  │ • Executive Summary (Manager)   │ │     │ • Formulates energy-saving plan    │  │
 │  │ • Developer Walkthrough (Dev)   │ │     │ • Rewrites code to be fast & green │  │
 │  │ • Production Docstring Generator│ │     └─────────────────┬──────────────────┘  │
 │  └─────────────────────────────────┘ │                       │                     │
 │                                      │                       ▼                     │
 │                                      │     ┌────────────────────────────────────┐  │
 │                                      │     │ AUTONOMOUS VERIFICATION LOOP       │  │
 │                                      │     │ • Does rewritten code parse?       │  │
 │                                      │     │ • Did Eco Score improve?           │  │
 │                                      │     │ • Self-reflects & re-tries if not  │  │
 │                                      │     └─────────────────┬──────────────────┘  │
 └──────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────┼─────────────────────┘
                                        │                       │
                                        ▼                       ▼
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │ STAGE 3: NEXT-GENERATION INTERACTIVE DASHBOARD                                     │
 │                                                                                    │
 │  1. Live Agent Thought Trace: Real-time status cards of all agents working         │
 │  2. Green Code Refactorer: Side-by-side Before vs. After code with diff viewer     │
 │  3. Verified Energy Jump: Eco Score 58/100 ➔ 94/100 (62% energy saved!)            │
 │  4. 3-in-1 Summary Suite: Toggle between Executive, Detailed, & Docstrings        │
 │  5. Physics-Based Moving PDG: Interactive draggable, zoomable network graph        │
 └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
========================================================================================
